"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.07073789946041398,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":68.3,"_gate_rev_durability":0.04480553914784746,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":47.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.07768389209943398,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":97.4,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.048209937942357506,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010893130981968167,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":81.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.0019400001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Ameriprise Financial, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a diversified financial services company in the United States and internationally. The company offers financial planning and advice services to individual and institutional clients. It operates through Advice & Wealth Management, Asset Management, Retirement & Protection Solutions, Corporate & Other segments. The Advice & Wealth Management segment provides financial planning and advice; brokerage products and services for retail and institutional clients; discretionary and non-discretionary investment advisory accounts; mutual funds; insurance and annuities products; cash management and banking products; and face-amount certificates. The Asset Management segment offers investment management, advice, and products to retail, high net worth, and institutional clients through third-party financial institutions, advisor network, direct retail, and its institutional sales force under the Columbia Threadneedle Investments brand name. Its products include U.S. mutual funds and their non-U.S. equivalents, exchange-traded funds, variable product funds underlying insurance, and annuity separate accounts; and institutional asset management products, such as traditional asset classes, separately managed accounts, individually managed accounts, collateralized loan obligations, hedge funds, collective funds, and property and infrastructure funds. The Retirement & Protection Solutions segment provides variable annuity products, as well as life and disability income insurance products to retail clients. Ameriprise Financial, Inc. was formerly known as American Express Financial Corporation and changed its name to Ameriprise Financial, Inc. in September 2005. The company was founded in 1894 and is based in Minneapolis, Minnesota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James M. Cracchiolo C.P.A. | Chairman & CEO | Age 66 | Compensation: $9.6M (FY2022)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $600K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $15K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Ameriprise Financial, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $45.1B market cap on $18.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 61% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 50-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $8.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 43 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.34\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Management returns a meaningful 7.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $29.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-29659643.81},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 61% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Critical Survey: Future FinTech Group (NASDAQ:FTFT) versus Ameriprise Financial (NYSE:AMP)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/critical-survey-future-fintech-group-nasdaqftft-versus-ameriprise-financial-nyseamp.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794590204.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ASX 200 AMP (ASX:AMP): Platform and Super Flows Must Keep Improving","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/retirement-planning/asx-200-amp-asxamp-platform-and-super-flows-must-keep-improving","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794564360.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"AMP (ASX:AMP) Shares in Focus: Why Is the ASX 200 Stock on the Radar?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/financial/amp-asxamp-shares-in-focus-why-is-the-asx-200-stock-on-the-radar","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794556800.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"AMP (ASX:AMP) Shares in Focus: Why Is the ASX 200 Stock Drawing Attention?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/financial/amp-asxamp-shares-in-focus-why-is-the-asx-200-stock-drawing-attention","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794556740.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.743,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"4,425 Ameriprise Financial, Inc. $AMP